  "finalReply": "Created reproducible build script at `/app/build.sh` producing bit-identical `/app/document.pdf`.\n\n**Script behavior:**\n- Hardcodes `/protected/document.tex`, `/protected/references.bib`, `/app/document.pdf`.\n- Validates `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` (warn + defaults to `date +%s` if missing/invalid), exports it with `FORCE_SOURCE_DATE=1`, `ZERO_AR_DATE=1`, `TZ=UTC`, `LC_ALL=C`, `LANG=C`.\n- Copies sources to fixed build dir `/app`, normalizes mtimes via `touch -d @${SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH}`, cleans `aux/bbl/blg/log/pdf`.\n- Runs `pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error -no-shell-escape` → `bibtex` (warn-and-continue on missing entries) → `pdflatex` → `pdflatex`, with explicit error exits for invalid LaTeX / missing sources / missing output.\n- Touches output PDF mtime to `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`.\n\n**Verification performed:**\n- `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=1234567890 /app/build.sh` twice → same MD5 `1481fed5b203694706f585cda923fe26`, `cmp` identical, `CreationDate (D:20090213233130Z)`.\n- Missing/invalid `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` → warns, exits 0, still builds PDF.\n- Different epoch (`9999999999`) → different `CreationDate`/hash, proving epoch control; restoring `1234567890` reproduces original hash.",
